    "shortDescription": "The Black Aluminium PN431 Figure 8 Descender belay device is a hardware tool used in activities such as rock climbing for belaying, rappelling, and descending. It\u2019s called so due to its shape, resembling the number 8, and is typically made of aluminium or steel with a central hole and two side slots. To use it, the rope is threaded through the central hole, then looped through one side slot and back through the opposite slot to form a bight. The rope is attached to the climber\u2019s harness using a locking karabiner, and tension is maintained on the brake strand while pulling the rope through the device to control the climber\u2019s speed. \u2022 To belay or lower a climber using the figure 8, the rope is pulled through the device while maintaining tension on the brake strand \u2022 By controlling the amount of tension on the brake strand, the belayer can control the speed at which the climber descends \u2022 Figure \u2013 eight descender, anodized. A traditional belay and rappelling device that is made from hot forged Al-alloy of high durability . \u2022 The ideal shape and size allows descending with one or two ropes . High strength forged aluminium. \u2022 Small hole can be used with thin ropes if necessary or as a belay plate Black Aluminium PN431 Figure 8 Descender.",
