    "shortDescription": "Suspension trauma safety straps are essential accessories for fall protection systems, designed to mitigate the risks associated with suspension trauma\u2014a condition that can occur when a person remains suspended in a harness for an extended period after a fall. These straps enable the suspended worker to stand in their harness, relieving pressure on the legs and promoting better blood circulation until rescue. \u2022 Allows the user to stand up in the harness, reducing pressure on the arteries and veins in the legs, thereby minimizing the risk of suspension trauma. \u2022 Designed to attach to most harness brands and styles, making them versatile for various fall protection setups. \u2022 The straps are unobtrusive during regular work activities and can be quickly deployed in the event of a fall. \u2022 Features a foolproof design that requires the user to unzip the packs and hook the straps \u2022 together with built-in hook and loop, facilitating rapid setup during emergencies.",
